 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S441-017\", \"clauses\": {\"read\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F05\", \"template\": \"Read the number {number} one place at a time, starting from the largest place.\", \"reasoning\": \"F05 is the only family whose text directs the learner to read a numeral. Its number slot prints digit values from 33 to 100 (printed_runs 33 to 100), so it addresses the clause through a hint rather than a question.\"}, \"write\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"Write the number: {word_form}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F16 appears in question_text and asks the learner to write a numeral from a word form. Its word_form values are observed from the generator's own word-form list and are in range 1 to 100.\"}, \"numerals\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F14\", \"template\": \"The number {number} is written in words as '{fill_value}'\", \"reasoning\": \"F14 prints the numeral itself in its number slot (printed_runs 33 to 100), so the learner works with numerals in the statement. It is a true or false style item nested in F15.\"}, \"up_to_100\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F05\", \"template\": \"Read the number {number} one place at a time, starting from the largest place.\", \"reasoning\": \"F05 prints numerals across the full range including the top of the bound (printed_runs reaches 90 to 100), so it produces problems at the upper limit of the declared range of 10 to 100.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F03\", \"F04\", \"F07\", \"F08\", \"F09\", \"F10\", \"F17\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Add the parts together to get {number}.\", \"Identify each word part and its {pv_label}.\", \"{capitalize}: {expanded_form}.\", \"{chunk}-{v}\", \"{p0}\", \"{v} hundred\", \"Write {number} in words.\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F03 (hint): the template asks the learner to add the parts together, and addition is in NOT_YET_KNOWN for this lc. F04 (hint): the nested F02 gate word value of each part gives the sentence Identify each word part and its value of each part, which is ungrammatical and does not state a task a grade 1 learner can follow. F07 (hint): the expanded_form domain prints sums joined with the plus operator, which is addition beyond this lc's gates; the capitalize slot inherits F01's gate word broken apart form. F08 (answer choices and keyed answer): chunk is drawn from the tens list and v from the ones list, both of which include the empty string and the teen words, so the template can produce a hyphen with a missing part or a tens word joined to a teen word, which are malformed number names. F09 (answer choices and keyed answer): p0 draws from the ones list and the tens list, both of which include the empty string, so the domain can produce a blank answer choice or a blank keyed answer. F10 (answer choices): the template v hundred with the ones list yields amounts above 100, outside the declared bound of 10 to 100. F17 (question): the template Write number in words asks the learner to write number names; the competency names numerals only, so this is outside its scope. The clauses are producible from F05, F14 and F16, which do not depend on the failing families.\"}",
